<p>R, G, and B values are printed in RGB888 format (DEC), C is a light value without processing, and RGB565 and RGB888 are HEX data printed in a certain format. LUX is light value processed. CT is color temperature. (<a target="_blank" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" class="external free" href="../../en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Color_temperature">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Color_temperature</a>) If you want to measure CT, please turn off the LED. INT is interrupted, 1: light value is over the threshold. <br />
You can turn the RGB value to color with <a target="_blank" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" class="external text" href="../../files.waveshare.com/upload/5/53/Infrared-Temperature-Sensor-Code">tools</a>:<br />
</p>
