					</div>
				</div>
</div>
<p><br />
</p>
<div class="panel-group">
				<div class="panel panel-default">
					<div class="panel-heading">
						<h4 class="panel-title">
							<a data-toggle="collapse" data-parent="#accordion" href="./TCS34725_Color_Sensor">
								Question: Modifying the integration time cannot trigger an interrupt or keep repeating the interrupt?

							</a>
						</h4>
					</div>
					<div id="accordion9" class="panel-collapse collapse in">
						<div class="panel-body">
<div>&#160;<b>Answer:</b></div>
<div>The interrupt is compared with the data in the Clear channel. The data in the Clear channel is related to the integration time. After actual measurement, the gain is 60 times. <br />
<p><a href="./File_TCS34725_Integrate_time.jpg" class="image"><img alt="TCS34725 Integrate time.jpg" src="../w/upload/thumb/8/87/TCS34725_Integrate_time.jpg/400px-TCS34725_Integrate_time.jpg" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="400" height="225" srcset="../w/upload/thumb/8/87/TCS34725_Integrate_time.jpg/600px-TCS34725_Integrate_time.jpg 1.5x, ../w/upload/thumb/8/87/TCS34725_Integrate_time.jpg/800px-TCS34725_Integrate_time.jpg 2x" /></a> <br />
Therefore, you should modify the threshold value if the sample rate is fast. And please increase the brightness of the LED when you set integrate time to 2.4ms.<br />
</p>
</div>
<div style="display:none;">{{{3}}}</div>
<div style="display:none;">{{{4}}}</div>
<p><font color="red" style="display:none;">{{{5}}}</font>
</p>
